From: MidG971 <midgy971@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: rock-3b: Model PI6C20100 as gated-fixed-clock

The Radxa ROCK 3B uses a PI6C20100 PCIe reference clock buffer to
provide 100MHz reference clocks to the PCIe 3.0 PHY and controllers.
This chip is currently modeled only as a fixed regulator
(vcc3v3_pi6c_03), with a phy-supply property on the pcie30phy node.

However, the PI6C20100 is a clock generator, not a power supply.
Model it properly as a gated-fixed-clock, following the pattern
established for the Rock 5 ITX and other boards with similar PCIe
clock buffer chips.

The regulator node is kept as-is since it controls the power supply
to the PI6C20100 chip via GPIO0_D4. The gated-fixed-clock node
references this regulator as its vdd-supply and provides a proper
100MHz clock output that the PCIe PHY and controllers can consume.

Signed-off-by: MidG971 <midgy971@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-rock-3b.dts | 23 ++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-rock-3b.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-rock-3b.dts
index XXXXXXX..XXXXXXX 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-rock-3b.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-rock-3b.dts
@@ -107,6 +107,16 @@
 		vin-supply = <&vcc3v3_sys>;
 	};

+	/* PI6C20100 PCIe reference clock buffer (100MHz) */
+	pcie30_refclk: pcie-clock-generator {
+		compatible = "gated-fixed-clock";
+		#clock-cells = <0>;
+		clock-frequency = <100000000>;
+		clock-output-names = "pcie30_refclk";
+		vdd-supply = <&vcc3v3_pi6c_03>;
+	};
+
 	/* PI6C PCIe clock generator chip power supply */
 	vcc3v3_pi6c_03: vcc3v3-pi6c-03-regulator {
 		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
@@ -152,8 +162,7 @@
 };

 /* PCIe 3.0 PHY - requires power supply for proper initialization */
 &pcie30phy {
-	phy-supply = <&vcc3v3_pi6c_03>;
 	status = "okay";
 };

